## 🔴 One: Five Core Rules

| # | Rule | Consequence of violation |
|---|------|--------------------------|
| 1 | Every "OK" claim must include command output as proof | Trust collapses immediately |
| 2 | Find one bug → scan entire system for same pattern | Fix one, miss three, never done |
| 3 | Before changing code → `grep -rn` all references | Change A breaks B |
| 4 | "Files updated" = files actually written, verified after | Claiming but not doing = deception |
| 5 | Dead code → delete immediately | Next session reads stale code, gets confused |

